cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RS-HW: Regime-Switching Short-Rate Dynamics. A Hidden Markov Approach to Hull-White Estimation on Euro-Area Government Bond Yields"
version: "1.0"
license: "MIT"
type: software
abstract: "Working paper and reproducible code. A two-state Gaussian hidden Markov model is fitted to daily changes of level, slope and curvature of 378 ECB euro-area AAA yield curves (2 January 2025 to 26 June 2026). A pre-registered exact rotation test of regime transitions against 26 economic events is not significant (p = 0.1088). Within the inferred regimes, Hull-White (Ornstein-Uhlenbeck) parameters of the 3-month rate are estimated with a BCa residual bootstrap: the volatility ratio is 2.66 (95% interval 2.22 to 3.40); mean reversion is not identified. Licences: code MIT; paper, documentation and author-compiled files CC BY 4.0; yield data subject to the ESCB reuse policy."
message: "If you use this software or the working paper, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - given-names: "Klaus Leopold"
    family-names: "von Moltke"
    affiliation: "DHBW Mannheim"
keywords:
  - regime switching
  - hidden Markov model
  - Hull-White model
  - Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process
  - term structure of interest rates
  - euro area
  - bootstrap
  - pre-registration
